findings.text:
Dead columns in the flat come through as exact zeros (the bad-pixel mask is applied later, in `stack.rs`), so `ff` is 0.0 for those pixels and this division writes `inf` into the science frame. Once an `inf` reaches the median combine it poisons the whole column. I would guard it here rather than rely on the mask running first:
```rust
let ff = *f / mean;
*px = if ff > f32::EPSILON { *px / ff } else { f32::NAN };
```
and let the combine skip NaNs, which it already does.

